Modifications to TheRobotStudio material
----------------------------------------
models/so101-camera-arm.glb (also embedded as base64 in docs/index.html) contains these
TheRobotStudio meshes, converted from STL to glTF, decimated to about 12% of their
triangles with meshoptimizer, merged per URDF link, placed in each link's frame from
so101_new_calib.urdf, and restyled:
  - base_so101_v2, base_motor_holder_so101_v1 (node base_link)
  - motor_holder_so101_base_v1, rotation_pitch_so101_v1 (node shoulder_link)
  - upper_arm_so101_v1 (node upper_arm_link)
  - under_arm_so101_v1, motor_holder_so101_wrist_v1 (node lower_arm_link)
  - wrist_roll_pitch_so101_v2 (node wrist_link)
  - sts3215_03a_v1, sts3215_03a_no_horn_v1 (nodes servo_1 to servo_5, used as a
    stand-in for the Hiwonder HX-30HM)
The gripper parts (moving jaw, fixed jaw / wrist_roll_follower, gripper servo) are not used.
Joint origins, axes and limits used by docs/index.html come from so101_new_calib.urdf.

Original to this project (not TheRobotStudio's): cad/riser_A_foot.stl,
cad/riser_B_top.stl, cad/camera_plate.stl, and the riser and camera plate in the glb.

